(Title) Tj
T*
(Feasibility of Comparing Empirical Antibiotic Regimens in Septic Intensive-Care Patients:) Tj
T*
(A Multi-Centre Adaptive Trial Evaluation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(The feasibility phase enrolled 200 of 284 screened critically ill patients with sepsis) Tj
T*
(across 10 intensive care units over a 5.5-month period. Participant demographic) Tj
T*
(characteristics showed a median age around 70 years, with approximately two-thirds males) Tj
T*
(and over 40% on mechanical ventilation at baseline. Four of five feasibility criteria were) Tj
T*
(met: recruitment achieved 70% of screened patients, protocol adherence exceeded 80%, data) Tj
T*
(availability for the primary outcome approached 86% by trial end \(though initially lagged) Tj
T*
(in early months\), and voluntary data withdrawal remained below 3%. The unmet criterion) Tj
T*
(regarding timely outcome ascertainment improved substantially in the final month,) Tj
T*
(approaching target thresholds. Thirty-day mortality was observed in approximately 30% of) Tj
T*
(randomised participants. Serious adverse reactions attributable to study medications) Tj
T*
(occurred in a small minority. These results support trial feasibility with a modification) Tj
T*
(focusing on outcome data capture processes. The randomised design, eligibility criteria,) Tj
T*
(and measurement approaches proved workable in routine intensive care settings.) Tj
T*
(Investigators concluded that a full-scale definitive trial comparing these empirical) Tj
T*
(antibiotics is justified.) Tj
